rota lap 4195, row 0 -- Aether, the row that hears; read the threshold page, Follow Our Compass, and The Lindy Effect. Aether asks why the work exists and listens for the silence where a claim used to be. Two silences answered this lap: a gate question left standing because nobody had measured it, and a finished lap of my own sitting in a stash nothing carried.
think Cold roster first, held still while it ran: 172 guards, 1889s, guards_red=2 -- standing_equipment and stash_record, one root. The evidence file named it plainly: records_unlanded, unlanded=1.
think Reds first, so the stash came before any new work. stash@{0}, parked by fleet_round_open at 20260907-163454, eight seconds before this lap opened, held session-logs/date/20260907/20260907-160828_the-fleet-page-run-before-it-was-written.kyri and seven other files. All three of the lap's new files were ABSENT from disk -- docs-geode/tutorials/running-the-fleet.md at 223 lines, the manual-and-docs-geode proposal, and the log itself.
think Restored the three new files with git checkout stash@{0} -- <paths>, then applied the four index edits by hand rather than by stash apply, since construction/ITINERARY.md and the shelf had both moved under a peer's rebase since the park. Two patched clean, two were hand-merged: the shelf front door's refresh line and tutorials row, and the day-shelf row.
think Graded the three restored pages before staging: running-the-fleet.md A+ 97, the proposal A+ 97, tutorials/README.md A+ 100. No molt frame forced.
think Then the lane's own open row. 20260907.144904 stands OPEN and its repair is gated on Keaton, with one stated objection: correcting Reach's read-past rule re-grades every page in one unmeasured step. Measuring is not correcting, so the measurement is agent-doable and it is the only thing between the row and its word.
think Built the pen copy: qa_report_card.sh with one line group replaced -- the elder /^[ \t]*[-*>#]/ rewritten to the four rules prose_register_scan.sh already runs (rule line, a bullet as marker-then-whitespace, quotes and headings, and the front-matter block recognised by position and shape together). Nothing else in the file moved.
obs THE CORRECTION IS NOT UNIFORMLY FAVORABLE, WHICH IS WHAT MAKES THE GATE QUESTION REAL. Over 429 living prose pages at one setting: 324 do not move, 56 rise, 49 fall. Mean composite delta +0.59; mean gain where it rose +7.70, mean loss where it fell -3.61. Sixteen pages cross up over B, seven cross down, and the under-B population goes 81 to 72.
obs REGISTER COMES BACK IDENTICAL ON ALL 429, and that is worth more than any delta. It is the proof the patch reaches one reading and leaves the other whole -- a patch that moved Register would have been reaching where it had no business.
obs THE SECOND HALF OF THE FAULT WAS NOT IN THE ROW. The elder rule drops body prose, which the row names; it also COUNTS front matter as prose, which nobody had measured. waymarks/stoa-300s/README.md is an index whose body is a table: Reach saw 13 words and 2 links -- the shared **Where this sits:** navigation line -- read 15 xrefs per 100 words against a budget of 3, floored Reach at 0, and graded the page D+ 69 on its own header. Corrected it reads A 94. Three STOA indexes and granary/README.md move exactly that way, and those are the largest movements in the corpus.
obs THE FALLS ARE HONEST, CHECKED BY OPENING TWO. ascii-first.md goes 330 to 548 counted words and grade 12 to 13; crypto/CONSTANT_TIME.md 670 to 735 and 11 to 12. In both the newly visible text is real body prose, and it is denser than the part the elder rule was reading. The meter has grown no harsher; it has started finishing the page.
obs I DID NOT APPLY THE FIX. The gate stands where the last lap left it, and a lap that crosses its own gate because it now likes the number has moved a ceiling by a side door. What this lap changes is that the word has arithmetic under it rather than an unknown.
obs THE BOUND BIT. The card sat at 40,920 of 40,960 and the new block ran 250 over on its first write; the elder shelved to construction/archive/20260907-171748_itinerary-landed-accounts.md and the block was cut five times to 40,949. The 8 x 2,048 that sized this bound is tight for a ship carrying both a landed lap and an open gate.
